{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/578162-beast-supernatural-hate","id":578162,"title":"[ Beast ] Supernatural Hate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-03T21:53:59-07:00","id":578162,"title":"[ Beast ] Supernatural Hate","content":"I'm sure this topic may have already been discussed somewhere in the 260+ pages of the Beast thread, but I wanted to have a tighter discussion about how Beasts would interact and be viewed by the other splats. Despite the Beast book suggesting that they would generally get along, things do not seem to be as rosy as they portray in the book.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampires -</b> The relation here seems mostly neutral, leaning towards the antagonistic the more that Vampires know about the nature of a Beast. That is to say, your average Vampire has no reason to know much of anything about a Beast and may consider them a useful supernatural asset since they are not really competing for any resources by default. But the more Vampires know about a Beast the more they are liable to be unhappy with the additional level of scrutiny that may come from investigating Heroes.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolves -</b> The relation here seems to be mostly negative. Beasts are going to create some serious negative resonance if they spend enough time in the same place as a werewolf, and the Werewolves are probably not going to be pleased cleaning up the mess that the Beast is not only making, but has very little awareness that they are making. An individual pack might agree to police that resonance issue in exchange for favors, but not many packs are going to want to do it for free.<br /> <br /> <b>Mages -</b> The relation here seems mostly neutral, leaning towards the side of pity. A mage would probably be fascinated by a Beast, and they have no reason to actively compete against each other for any resources, so there is nothing actively positive or negative about the relationship. However, Mages might feel that Beasts are a useful tool to be cultivated or destroyed because of their ability to use their Skeleton Key to explore new places (once the Mage has detected them), break through into enemy realms, or possibly fear that their own realms could be broken into. There are too many different kinds of mages to anticipate how they might react as a whole, except to say that they are liable to view the Beast as a useful or dangerous weapon and not a person.<br /> <br /> <b>Changelings -</b> The relation here seems to be dramatically negative. Things may change once Changeling 2E is released so this may no longer be true, but based on the 1E Changelings a Beast is going to remind them too much of the abusers that they have escaped. While some may accept this and fall into the cycle of abuse they are so familiar with (and maybe even crave), the vast majority of changelings are probably going to ostracize and stay the hell away from the Beast. Especially once they realize that the Beast can possibly follow them through realms, violating their already delicate sense of personal space and safety.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunters - </b>The relation here seems to be mostly negative. Hunters are going to see Beasts as the monsters they are, and in general are not going to want to cooperate or coexist unless that Beast is offering something pretty solid to the Hunters in question. More importantly, Hunters seem like they could easily become involved with Heroes and join forces to track down a beast. Even if they are hesitant about the some of the bullshit a Hero is saying, they might still use that Hero to finish their own hunt for a Beast. More disturbing, is it possible for Heroes to outright join Hunter societies and form entire cabals of Heroes with Hunter assets?<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts? What about some of the other supernatural splats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 07-04-2015, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T01:33:10-07:00","id":578400,"title":"","content":"Vampires- Heroes aren't any particular threat to the masquerade, heroes don't investigate they track with their built in beast sense, and the book flat out mentions that a hero isn't going to know what a vampire is unless they start doing something obvious like baring fangs. <br /> <br /> You've also apparently forgotten that elder vampires need to start looking for alternate food sources when humans stop counting, not only do beasts count as a valid alternate food source, but so do heroes. So an elder vampire can get food that is nice enough to deliver itself as well as an ally that can make their powers stronger, win win. <br /> <br /> Werewolf- Werewolves only care about resonance when it causes spirits to get frisky, spirits that can feed by just hanging out with a beast is a spirit that doesn't need to urge or possess someone to get their daily bread. Spirits are also just as valid targets for prey or punishment as anyone else, so there are beasts who can feed by directly by helping werewolves hunt, even without family dinner. <br /> <br /> Changeling- I won't argue with the fact that Beasts claim kinship with the keepers is going to upset more than a few changelings, there are also going to be plenty of changelings who like the thought of feeding their keepers, loyalists, privateers, hostile hobgoblins, psycho fetches, etc, to a friendly dragon. For less trusting changelings, beasts arent immune to oaths.<br /> <br /> Hunter- Hunters, by and large, aren't fond of serial killers, which is what those heroes who slay beasts are, a typical hunter is probably going to assume that a hero is a particularly delusional slasher, and act accordingly. As for hunter relationships with beasts, that really all depends. Many hunters aren't of the &quot;it's not human, kill it til it dies&quot; mentality. Some hunters hunt criminals, so do some beasts, so beasts and hunters can form their own hunter parties. The AO include diplomats to supernaturals, who better to approach then the &quot;sticks their noses in everyone's business&quot; beasts? Also, since kinship applies to lucifuge or otodo, a beast can be a source of help or information to members of those conspiracies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T02:33:13-07:00","id":578471,"title":"","content":"Beside StSword great arguments, I have also one more.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/578162-beast-supernatural-hate?p=578400#post578400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Vampires- You've also apparently forgotten that elder vampires need to start looking for alternate food sources when humans stop counting, not only do beasts count as a valid alternate food source, but so do heroes. So an elder vampire can get food that is nice enough to deliver itself as well as an ally that can make their powers stronger, win win.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does not Mother's Kiss mean that vampire drinking the beast can get bonus to using his Disciplines for a scene? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-06-2015, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T06:55:53-07:00","id":578687,"title":"","content":"That being said, if you want conflict between beasts and other supernaturals, it's not hard to imagine.<br /> <br /> Kinship is a two edged sword when it comes to crossovers. <br /> <br /> In a vampire game, the beast you meet might already have kinship with Belial's Brood, VII, druagr. or the strix.<br /> <br /> In a werewolf game, the beast could claim kinship with the pure, balehounds, spirits, hosts, or claimed.<br /> <br /> In mage, the mad, reapers, scelesti, and other left hand types.<br /> <br /> Promethean- Centimani and pandorans.<br /> <br /> Changelings- Privateers, loyalists, the soulless, hostile hobgoblins, true fae.<br /> <br /> Hunter- Well duh, they claim kinship with pretty much everything hunters tend to hunt, barring regular criminals, I'd throw in cultists with dread powers in the mostly human kin category.<br /> <br /> Geists- Sanctified, abmortals, wretched, kerberoi, or the vacant.<br /> <br /> Mummy- the deceived, and the lifeless in greater and lesser categories.<br /> <br /> Demon- cryptids<br /> <br /> So yeah whether a beast in a crossover game is the players best friend or archnemesis will completely depend on the beast in question. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T08:21:48-07:00","id":578778,"title":"","content":"I don't get the point of this. Are we trying to find reasons for them to fight? Not fight? Every interaction is going to be based on individual circumstances, contexts, and personalities of those involved. Generalities are pretty worthless at best, and actively harmful to game play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T09:44:19-07:00","id":578876,"title":"","content":"My planned mage is a (non-beast specific) hero. I mean this in the generic English language way. If things are killing people he will stop them because he is a hero. He has the persona merit and his persona is a hero. If beasts are messing with humans then he will stop them. If the messing involves multiple killings then they are high up on the list. If it involves giving them bad dreams then they're so far down the list he'll never get to them. But given some beasts do have a need to kill (or so I'm told) then my mage will definitely be in conflict with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6710-taccom","name":"TacCom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T18:12:58-07:00","id":579302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/578162-beast-supernatural-hate?p=578778#post578778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get the point of this. Are we trying to find reasons for them to fight? Not fight? Every interaction is going to be based on individual circumstances, contexts, and personalities of those involved. Generalities are pretty worthless at best, and actively harmful to game play.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're trying to establish generalities, stereotypes and first impressions, because that is what society runs on. Individuality and exceptions come later, after the Beast has proven himself and gotten over initial hurdles (some have it easier than others).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T05:07:53-07:00","id":579729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/578162-beast-supernatural-hate?p=579302#post579302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're trying to establish generalities, stereotypes and first impressions, because that is what society runs on. Individuality and exceptions come later, after the Beast has proven himself and gotten over initial hurdles (some have it easier than others).</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bI haven't checked the updated stuff yet, too much to do, but the original kickstarter really did talk about this stuff. Starting on page 311, Beasts in the World of Darkness. We've got how Beasts see others, and how the others see back. That's our generalities, right there. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-05-2015, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T06:01:45-07:00","id":579739,"title":"","content":"Plus, the Begotten cheat; they naturally start with a good impression with any Kin. It's a part of their template.<br /> Monsters magically like them until the Beast screws it up.<br /> <br /> Seriously. &quot;Thicker Than Water&quot; in chapter 3, I think.<br /> You aren't allowed to immediately dislike Beasts unless you're God-Machine related or mundane (most Hunters don't qualify as kin, and are therefore mundane).<br /> Negative feelings require interaction; initial impression is to give them the benefit of the doubt. It's not even contested.<br /> <br /> Best mind whammy power ever. How else can a game be cross-over friendly in any WoD. Everybody who has their stuff together is absolutely paranoid! Instant trust is the only way they don't eliminate you just to be safe.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T06:13:48-07:00","id":579743,"title":"","content":"And lets not forget that Beasts are built to be not only synergetic, but actively beneficial.<br /> <br /> A vampire out on a hunt? The Begotten can enhance the vampire's powers, and distract onlookers, just for the benefit of watching them feed like a voyeur. Beasts can really boost a werewolf pack's chance at a spirit hunt, plus not needing to take part of the essence from the &quot;kill.&quot; Mages would adore working with Beasts. Simply sharing supernatural secrets not only helps with the Mage's desire for Mysteries, but fulfills the Beast's Hunger as well; and tha'ts before the explorations that can expand the Lair and Gnosis both. Changelings are abuse victims and, like all abuse victims, have a tendency to bond strongly with those they trust, and Beasts have a very strong edge when it comes to earning that trust with Thicker than Water.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, while its true there's plenty of reasons for the interaction between supernaturals and Beasts to go south, in general the reaction should be positive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T06:14:49-07:00","id":579744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/578162-beast-supernatural-hate?p=579729#post579729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bI haven't checked the updated stuff yet, too much to do, but the original kickstarter really did talk about this stuff. Starting on page 311, Beasts in the World of Darkness. We've got how Beasts see others, and how the others see back. That's our generalities, right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The purpose of the thread is to establish non-positive generalities and stereotypes on the part of other supernaturals; Beast sort of assumes a positive relationship because of Kinship, which may lack nuance. This is, essentially, a thread with the intent of explaining the reasons supernaturals might be ill-disposed towards Beasts, rather than axiomatically choosing and being well-disposed towards Beasts (this seems particularly weird for hunters, who devote a weird proportion of their word-count to hunting Heroes for monster hunters in a game about monsters); this does not imply that a positive relationship cannot exist, but allows for greater nuance on a wide scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T06:56:26-07:00","id":579793,"title":"","content":"Nuance is possible but the fact is, under bad circumstances, Beasts do better than any other stranger. Points of Conflict is one thing, negative stereotypes are another.<br /> In particular, the splat is built to prevent such things. The generalities are issues that pop up frequently but in order to be a point of contention requires actually knowing the Begotten, either personally or through someone else.<br /> <br /> That said; most Hunters aren't Kin. They generally don't benefit from Thicker Than Water. Beasts are just another monster in the night. They shouldn't have any problems when lacking negative opinions. Only some of the Conspiracies count as Kin after all. (Offically only the Lucifuge has been called out so far; TF:V, VASCU, AKD &amp; the Knights of Adrian have all been called out as not-Kin)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T07:04:38-07:00","id":579798,"title":"","content":"Other monsters don't really start &quot;liking&quot; them so much as usually being inclined to see them in a non-negative light in their first encounter. By logic, there are a number of things that could shake up that first impression, so it's not nearly as absolute or powerful as some people make it sound like.<br /> <br /> And the existing text does already point out plenty of potential negative threads between Beasts and other supernaturals. That is a thing that is accounted for in the presentation of Beast The Primordial, and the rest entirely comes down to individual personalities and circumstances of interaction. There's no lack of nuance there, far as I can see.<br /> <br /> (@Keter: The vast majority of Hunters also are not influenced at all by Thicker Than Water, so you're wrong there. This is why relations between Hunters and the Begotten tend to result in more of what interactions between Hunters and monsters <i>usually do. </i>The reason the book dedicates a significant amount of space talking about the possible antagonism or lack thereof between Heroes and Hunters is because their similarities and differences make for more complex relations between them than between Hunters and Beasts overall. Because the meaning Heroes may have for Hunters is of greater significance than that of Beasts - and by extension other monsters -, and this is without taking into account what the myriad of individual circumstances and egos involved may result in for their interactions.)<br /> <br /> I feel like some people are also conflating the idea that every other supernatural will like Beasts with the far more accurate and to the point matter that <i>Beasts almost uniformly have practical and personal interest in fostering good relationships with other monsters.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-05-2015, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T10:31:43-07:00","id":579948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/578162-beast-supernatural-hate?p=579744#post579744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The purpose of the thread is to establish non-positive generalities and stereotypes on the part of other supernaturals;</div> </div> </div> </div> Those paragraphs on page 311 include negative aspects as well as positive. My point remains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T15:30:31-07:00","id":581576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/578162-beast-supernatural-hate?p=579739#post579739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, the Begotten cheat; they naturally start with a good impression with any Kin. It's a part of their template.<br /> Monsters magically like them until the Beast screws it up.<br /> <br /> Seriously. &quot;Thicker Than Water&quot; in chapter 3, I think.<br /> You aren't allowed to immediately dislike Beasts unless you're God-Machine related or mundane (most Hunters don't qualify as kin, and are therefore mundane).<br /> Negative feelings require interaction; initial impression is to give them the benefit of the doubt. It's not even contested.<br /> <br /> Best mind whammy power ever. How else can a game be cross-over friendly in any WoD. Everybody who has their stuff together is absolutely paranoid! Instant trust is the only way they don't eliminate you just to be safe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are making the mistake of using the dictionary definition of &quot;good impression&quot;, not the WoD rules specific definition.<br /> In the Social Maneuvering rules, Impressions govern exactly one thing: time between rolls to open doors.<br /> Despite its name, impression has absolutely zero effect on your actual chances of influencing someone. It doesn't make the actual diceroll for opening doors more likely to succeed or affect the number of doors. The only thing it does is make you succeed or fail faster.<br /> <br /> The good impression effect doesn't even insure that you get to roll at all, as Impression only comes into play during phase 3 of Social Maneuvering (Impression). If your ST decides during Step 1 (Goals) that your Goal is unreasonable given the facts of the situation, then the encounter fails before you ever get to the point where you could apply that higher frequency of door opening rolls. So no Beasts waltzing up to Werewolves a day after killing half their pack with the Goal of making them your friend: the ST will tell you &quot;unreasonable Goal&quot; and you get ripped apart before Good Impression has any chance to affect the situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 07-06-2015, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T22:27:42-07:00","id":581963,"title":"","content":"Oh something that is bound to cause friction between beasts and other supernaturals- using their innate ability to pretend to be another type of monster.<br /> <br /> I mean seriously, you're a changeling/vampire/werewolf/mage/whatever, you find out your relationship with your buddy is predicated on a lie. What are the odds you're just going to laugh it off?<br /> <br /> Or even worse, a beast joined an organization under false pretenses, what are the odds that the local carthaginians, winter court, mysterium, etc, aren't going to blow a fuse? <br /> <br /> Other than prometheans, of course, I imagine they'd just be happy to find someone who doesn't hate them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}